## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical skills in dynamic per-tenant API version routing, assessing candidates' knowledge of Redis-backed routing state, Traefik dynamic configuration, and Docker-based edge proxies across distributed infrastructure.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant version routing
- Redis-backed configuration store (tenant_id → api_version)
- Traefik dynamic configuration via Docker provider
- Sidecar pattern for pushing configuration updates
- Multi-datacenter consistency and TLS edge handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sidecar that watches Redis and updates Traefik rules
async function syncRoutes(redis, docker) {
  const routes = await redis.hgetall('tenant:versions');
  for (const [tenantId, version] of Object.entries(routes)) {
    await updateTraefikRule(docker, tenantId, version);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-DC data residency controls, real-time policy updates, and secure audit logging in a docker-dca setup.

## Key Concepts
- Data residency and cross-DC egress policies
- WASM-based per-tenant policy engine (Wasmtime)
- Vault-driven tenant configs and SPIFFE SVID rotation
- SIEM-based auditing and reproducible bootstrap

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluation sketch
function evaluate(event, tenant) {
  if (event.destDC === 'DC-B' && !tenant.optIn) return 'block';
  redact(event.payload, tenant.schema);
  return 'allow';
}
```

